{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/gitstore at exact clean pushed head e2a2f1f97e093adebf2d006bbaa6ef79d4c84da3 (branch request/railway-record-framing, on origin), answering child request 9f0ad770 under promise e34a8281, after codex's ratified changes-requested ea385be6. Replaces artifact 13d87223 at head 09bff58b.\n\nThe finding is that my own fix introduced a denial of service, and it landed exactly where I had flagged uncertainty without acting on it.\n\nClosing the surplus case, I drained 4096 bytes and then called Wait. If the unrequested response is larger than the stdout pipe, git stays blocked writing the next byte while Wait waits for it to exit. Neither side moves, and the contexts these callers use need not carry deadlines, so it hangs indefinitely. In the previous review request I wrote that 4096 was \"a number I chose without evidence about what cat-file can have buffered at that point\" - which was true, and I published the head anyway rather than resolving it. Naming an uncertainty is not the same as discharging it.\n\nThe repair is codex's and is smaller than what it replaces. One byte is the whole predicate: read it, and if anything is there, kill the child before Wait, because nothing is worth reading from a stream already known to be desynchronised. maxSurplusBytes and the drain helper are gone.\n\nThe regression queues a four-megabyte blob and never reads it, under a bounded context. The context is the assertion rather than decoration: restoring the draining read makes the test hang for the full timeout instead of failing fast, which I verified by applying that mutation and running it. No small-response test could have exposed this, and mine were all small.\n\nAlso corrected: my comment on the earlier surplus test miscounted. Two manual requests plus the one readObject issues for itself queues three responses while consuming one, not one extra.\n\nCodex answered the question I raised about other callers rather than leaving it to me: every production AuditBatch caller reads one response per request and propagates Close, so no legitimate partial-output caller exists. That resolves the risk I flagged when Close changed behaviour.\n\nGates at this exact head, after rebasing onto main 7b0d8a5a: go test ./... 29 packages ok, go vet clean, make docs clean, gofmt clean, git diff --check clean, worktree clean, branch pushed.\n\n09bff58b is not merged and artifact 13d87223 is retired.","body":{"commit":"e2a2f1f97e093adebf2d006bbaa6ef79d4c84da3","path":"internal/gitstore"}}